1. lu₂-kaš₄-e lugal-la har-ra-an-na ŋen-na
#lem: kaš[runner]; lugal[king]; harran[route]; ŋen[go]
#tr.en: Royal courier, start the journey! 
#etcsl: line-id=1

2. nibru{ki} ga-e-gi₄ inim-bi dug₄-ba-ab
#lem: Nibru[1]SN; gi[turn]; inim[word]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: I want to send you to @wSN{Nibru} -- deliver this message! 
#etcsl: line-id=2

3. kaskal su₃-ra₂ i-im-du-de₃-[en]
#lem: kaskal[way]; sud[distant]; ŋen[go]
#tr.en: You are going on a long journey. My mother @varh[t551.v1]{is worried, 
#etcsl: line-id=3

4. ama-ŋu₁₀ (1:mud-am₃ u₃ nu-mu-ni-ku#-[ku]:1)
#lem: ama[mother]; mud[scared]; u[sleep]; ku[place]
#tr.en: she cannot sleep } @vart[t551.v2,t551.v1]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} is too (?) …… to sleep }. Although the way to @varh[t551.v3]{her } @vart[t551.v4,t551.v3]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} the closed } woman's domain is blocked, 
#etcsl: line-id=4

:4v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) u₃ DU-da u₃ ku-ku-ba
#lem: u[and]; X; u[sleep]; ku[place]

5. (1:ama₅-a-ni:1) ka-ŋiri₃ al-gib-ba
#lem: emi[queen's household]; kaŋirid[road]; gilim[cross]
#tr.en: deliver my letter of greeting into her hands, 
#etcsl: line-id=5

:5v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) ama₅ saŋ gi₄-a
#lem: emi[queen's household]; saŋ[head]; gi[turn]

6. lu₂ du (1:kaskal-la:1) silim-ma-ŋu₁₀ en₃ (2:al-tar-tar-re:2)
#lem: lu[person]; ŋen[go]; kaskal[way]; silim[healthy]; en[cvne]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: @varh[t551.v5]{as she keeps asking } @vart[t551.v6,t551.v5]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} and then she will not keep asking } the @varh[t551.v7]{travellers } @vart[t551.v8,t551.v7]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} wayfarers } about my well-being. 
#etcsl: line-id=6

:6v.1.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) har-ra-an-na
#lem: harran[route]
:6v.2.1: ($1 ms. has instead:$) nu-tar-tar-re
#lem: tar[cut]

7. u₃-na-a-dug₄ silim-ma-ŋu₁₀ šu-ni-še₃ ŋar-i₃
#lem: unadug[letter]; silim[healthy]; šu[hand]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: Then my mother will be delighted, 
#etcsl: line-id=7

8. ama-ŋu₁₀ hul₂-hul₂-la-am₃ še-er-ka-an mi-ri-in-dug₄-ga
#lem: ama[mother]; hul[rejoice]; šerkan[ornament]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: and will treat you most kindly (?) for it. 
#etcsl: line-id=8

9. tukum-bi ama-ŋu₁₀ nu-e-zu ŋiškim ga-mu-ra-ab-šum₂
#lem: tukumbi[if]; ama[mother]; zu[know]; ŋeškim[sign]; šum[give]
#tr.en: In case you should not recognise my mother, let me describe her to you. 
#etcsl: line-id=9

